---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site, localBusinessSchema } from '../../config/site';

const procedureSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "MedicalProcedure",
  "name": "Tooth-Colored Fillings – DFW Metroplex",
  "description": "Need to address a cavity? At Bear Creek Family Dentistry, we can restore your oral health with tooth-colored fillings in DFW Metroplex.",
  "procedureType": "https://schema.org/Therapeutic",
  "provider": {
    "@type": "Dentist",
    "name": "Bear Creek Family Dentistry",
    "address": {
      "@type": "PostalAddress",
      "addressLocality": "Dallas"
    }
  }
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Tooth-Colored Fillings Dallas | ${site.name}`}
  description="Need to address a cavity? At Bear Creek Family Dentistry, we can restore your oral health with tooth-colored fillings in DFW Metroplex."
  schema={[localBusinessSchema, procedureSchema]}
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 md:py-24">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-brand-primary mb-4">
      <a href="/services" class="hover:underline">Services</a>
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-neutral-dark mb-4 leading-tight">
      Tooth-Colored Fillings – DFW Metroplex
    </h1>
    <p class="text-xl text-neutral-mid mb-8 leading-relaxed">
      Need to address a cavity? At Bear Creek Family Dentistry, we can restore your oral health with tooth-colored fillings in DFW Metroplex.
    </p>
    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-neutral-mid leading-relaxed">
      <p class="mb-4">Years ago, repairing cavities meant using silver amalgam fillings. These not only stood out visually but could also pose risks to your oral health over time. Thankfully, dental technology has come a long way. Fillings are used to restore tooth structure damaged by decay, and composite resin has become a superior alternative to metal. This advanced material consists of a putty-like mixture that bonds directly with tooth enamel, allowing us to preserve more of your natural tooth structure while creating a restoration that blends seamlessly with your smile. Beyond aesthetics, composite resin offers functional benefits — its biocompatible nature means it works with your tooth rather than just sitting on top of it.</p>
      
    </div>
    <div class="mt-10 flex gap-4 flex-wrap">
      <a href="/schedule" class="btn-primary">Book Your Visit</a>
      <a href="/services" class="btn-secondary">View All Services</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pb-16 md:pb-24">
    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-neutral-mid leading-relaxed space-y-4">
      <p>Made from a putty-like mixture of ultra-fine acrylic and glass particles.</p>
      <p>Composite resin bonds directly with tooth enamel, preserving more natural tooth structure than metal fillings.</p>
      <p>Procedure is often completed in a single appointment, typically about an hour.</p>
      <p>The area is numbed to ensure comfort before the procedure begins.</p>
      <p>Decayed tissue is removed and the tooth is thoroughly cleaned before the filling is applied.</p>
      <p>A composite resin shade is carefully selected to match natural enamel.</p>
      <p>Resin is applied in layers; a curing light hardens and bonds the material securely to the tooth.</p>
      <p>The filling is polished for a smooth finish and bite is checked.</p>
      <p>Composite resin forms a tight seal with enamel, reducing dental sensitivity.</p>
      <p>Seals out bacteria, lowering chances of further decay or infection.</p>
      <p>Available for both adults and children.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
